Tokenization is the process of breaking down natural language into tokens, or small pieces of information such as morphemes or words. In NLP (Natural Language Processing), tokenization represents a major step in understanding a sentence or a block of text. Apart from words and phrases, tokenization can also include symbols, punctuation and special characters. Tokenization also comprises various techniques, such as Sentence Tokenization, Word Tokenization, White Space Tokenization etc.

For example, if you provide the sentence "Please, do not cross this line" as the input, the tokenizer would output [Please, do, not, cross, this, line].

There are several tools that allow developers to tokenize the text. Among them, there is the Natural Language Toolkit (nltk) in Python, that provides several tokenizing functions. For instance, there's the WhitespaceTokenizer and WordPunctTokenizer classes for text tokenization
