Embeddings are a way to represent categorical data as dense vectors in a continuous vector space. In NLP, embeddings are used to represent words as vectors. These vectors can capture the semantic and syntactic properties of words. Word embeddings are learned during the training process of a NLP model.

In NLP models, embeddings are used in the input layer of the model. The input to the model is a sequence of words, and each word is represented as an embedding vector. These embedding vectors are then used as input to the rest of the model.

