The Gaussian Error Linear Unit (GELU) is used as an activation function in Transformer architectures for NLP models.
It aims to tackle the "dying ReLU" problem (where many neurons in a network could be inactive due to negative inputs), thus encouraging the network to learn more complex and meaningful representations.

One of the reasons why GELU is preferred over other activation functions (like ReLU) in Transformers is its ability to handle a higher proportion of negative inputs with a smoother output around zero, preserving valuable information and reducing information loss.

