---------------------------------------------

`generate_with_streaming()` is a simple way to make the generation bindings
[streaming][].

By default, generation bindings generate all the DBIC results at once.
This may become a performance bottleneck in applications that have large
amounts of data they need to generate. In such cases, it may be useful to
use generation bindings in conjunction with [DBIx::Class::ResultSource::Streaming][]
to stream the loading and generation.

### Why?

"Internally, the ResultSource knows what SQL will be required to search for
a single row definition in the result set, or the definitions for a range of
consecutive rows ... "

~DBIx::Class::ResultSource::Streaming docs

Streaming is not only about performance, it also allows you to do sections
on very large [`resultsets()`][Result Set] within the result source with no
memory effects at all.

### Basic usage

Given dataset and bind gen for mod1 a very lengthy and repetitive dataset.

	$dataset = [
	    { foo => 1, bar => 1 },
	    { foo => 2, bar => 2 },
	    ...       0.o
	];

