[173/200] Running: What causes generation to stall midway?...

🧠 LLM Response:


Generation should not stall momentarily, if so please check the control box. Sometimes, if the nozzle clogs, this could also cause a momentary stopping of the generator. After about 30 seconds the generator will start up again.

An overcharged battery may also cause this problem. Therefore, after 5 hours of generating, one should disconnect the generator if the battery is completely charged.

It is also possible that the pump may be faulty or damaged. Look carefully at the pump and see if it turns freely. If not, it is necessary to purchase a new pump. Doing so would solve the problem.

1. Why does the generator have trouble starting?

The C2M3 can have trouble starting if the control box is damaged, if the board needs resetting, if the battery terminals are corroded, or if the wires are loose. Please also make sure that the bottom of the generator faces towards the sun.

You may also need to reset the control box. To do this, slide the indicator at the bottom of the back panel to 3rd (off) position. Disconnect the battery with the black wire off first, then the white wire. Wait for 15 seconds. Then plug the battery back in.

Corrosion, loose terminals and faulty wires can impede the flow of electricity to the control box which is essential for the generator to start.

2. Will I ever need to replace my pump, control box or diverter valve?

Over time, with normal, daily use, parts of the system can become damaged, corroded, or clogged. Typically the parts that might need replacement are the: pumps, control boxes and diverter valves. For this reason, we carry spare parts and would be happy to replace them for you. Call or email us at support@solarliquidfuel.com or 510.859.5000 during business hours.

3. Will my generator work in the rain or snow?

The generator is designed for outdoor use in a covered area such as a carport and is sealed from the elements, so you should have no trouble using it in rain or snow. However, do not put the generator in standing water. The generator can not be used upside down.

Note: To increase efficiency in colder months, we recommend first covering the panels with a clear material, which will increase the heat given off to the panels and increase output.

4. Will my generator charge in overcast conditions?

The panels can generate power even on cloudy days, but are most effective when in direct sunlight. The generator should still produce enough electricity to operate comfortably.

5. Will the generator overcharge my battery?

The generator is equipped with an overcharge safety. If the generator senses too high of a current it will automatically shut down the pump so that the battery does not overcharge. Thus, the battery will not be damaged.

6. How long will my generator last?

The generator will last 20 years or more.

7. How long will my block last?

The block should last 1-3 years depending on its conditions of storage and use.

8. Will my generator produce enough power for an air conditioning unit?

Our generators are not strong enough to power an air conditioning unit.

9. Is the generator water-tight?

Yes, the generator is water-tight.

If there are further questions or concerns that have not been addressed, please give us a call or email.

Tel: 510.859.5000

