#### token\_logprobs

A list of dictionaries containing:

* index — token index indicating position in outputs.
* logprob — the negative log probability of that token.

This field isn't returned by default. In order to get token logprobs, include \
`logprobs=true` in the `/completions` qs parameter.

The `token_logprobs` provided in the return are the, possibly modified,
identifier of the token. Note that this is not a locale SLUG but
the internal token unique string form of the token. Doing a `POST
/completions` with this value oftentimes will return unrelated tokens.

Also note that logprobs are costly to calculate relative to just returning the
top token. The number of `token_logprobs` able to be returned will be less
than the large `max_tokens` parameter requests since the large number of tokens
also increases the calculation cost, therefore limiting the range of tokens that
can have their negative log probabilities calculated.


