When you create an `HF` (i.e., Half Float) object, and call its `generate()` method, it performs interpolation and generates a raw image buffer, see [capture application source code](https://github.com/mofixz/HalfFloat/blob/master/cpp/src/hf_generate.cc#L50).

Note: This is for HalfFloat 1.x.

One-by-one:

- `to_raw_image` is getter for raw image buffer. It allocates raw image's memory space and stores the raw image in [libraw](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/LibRaw/LibRaw) image struct.

- `interpolate()` is the method to do interpolation, importing the result into a raw image buffer.

    `interpolate()` also does RAW format -> RGB format type conversion, because the raw image buffer contains uncompressed and unprocessed pixel data in RAW image format.

    The RAW format -> RGB format type conversion is done via processing the image data on CPU by using `unpack()` and `bsraw_unpack_linear()`  according to image metadata [which is extracted from RAW/DNG metadata](https://github.com/mofixz/HalfFloat/blob/master/cpp/src/hf_generate.cc#L77).

- `filgrain_decoder.DecodeNewNoise()`: see its [definition](https://github.com/mofixz/HalfFloat/blob/master/cpp/src/filgrain_decoder.cc), which reads "filmgrain noise" ([filmgrain](App/Filmgrain.md) for more) data in DNG file header. Once the noise data is read, the `filigrain_decoder` object is deleted.

    Note that the [Github address](https://github.com/mofixz/HalfFloat/blob/master/cpp/src/filgrain_decoder.cc#L58) of the original author contains the [filmgrain library](https://github.com/mofixz/libfilgrain-fusion), which is itself a half float picture interpolation algorithm.

- `libexport.SaveImageProcessed()`: Saving the generated RGB.

    > Saving the picture is only processed when consumer sets the `save_image` argument in `HF` object.

    Save the raw image into `output.png`, with the RGB format type stored via the [raw image buffer](https://github.com/mofixz/HalfFloat/blob/master/cpp/src/hf_generate.cc#L144), and save it in `.png` format.

Before `HF::generate()`, you should call `HF::Open()` to load DNG metadata, and `HF::LoadProcessParams()` to load preprocessing settings.

Since this implementation uses OpenCV 3.0, you need to binding OpenCV to the correct version.

Explain the optimized internals of HF `generate()` loop. (HF >= 2.0)

Based on the source code in [capture application source code](https://github.com/open-quantum-safe/tweag_half Float/blob/master/cpp/src/hf_generate.cc#L86), the optimized internals of HF `generate()` loop performs roughly the same steps as in 1.x, only that more GPU acceleration is used.

First critical factor: in HF 1.x, the interpolation and the postprocessing are in series.  In HF 2.x via GPU acceleration, the interpolation processing and postprocessing do not run serially. It places the process of interpolation and postprocessing in different pipeline stages to provide better overall performance.

The second critical factor: In HF 2.x, we use [OpenCV GPU acceleration](https://docs.opencv.org/master/d6/d6a/tutorial_gpu_basics.html) in the pipeline we use [OpenCV DNN implementation](https://docs.opencv.org/master/d3/df7/tutorial_dnn.html).

